WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.745 --> 00:00:17.010
The holiday season is busy for cab drivers and their horses.

2
00:00:18.231 --> 00:00:22.593
People rush about to parties and balls, and nobody wants to walk in the chilly weather.

3
00:00:25.154 --> 00:00:29.196
Jerry was glad for the extra work, though the cough he'd had last winter returned.

4
00:00:32.908 --> 00:00:37.031
When New Year's Eve arrived, a pair of men hired him to take them to a party.

5
00:00:39.233 --> 00:00:41.655
We dropped them off at a fancy house at nine o'clock.

6
00:00:41.675 --> 00:00:45.338
"Come pick us up at eleven," one of the men directed.

7
00:00:45.358 --> 00:00:47.039
"But it's a card party.

8
00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:51.103
If we're not finished with our game, you might have to wait a few minutes."

9
00:00:55.066 --> 00:00:56.287
Jerry was always punctual.

10
00:00:56.847 --> 00:00:59.029
At eleven o'clock we were back in front of the house.

11
00:01:00.550 --> 00:01:02.332
The party was still going on inside.

12
00:01:03.564 --> 00:01:05.846
Fifteen minutes passed, and then thirty.

13
00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:10.790
By the time the clock chimed twelve, the door still hadn't opened.

14
00:01:12.392 --> 00:01:13.933
It was a cold, windy evening.

15
00:01:16.435 --> 00:01:19.678
As we stood waiting, the rain started and quickly turned to sleet.

16
00:01:21.039 --> 00:01:24.402
Jerry covered me with my blanket, but there was no shelter for him.

17
00:01:27.224 --> 00:01:31.608
He walked up and down the block, trying to keep warm, but that made him cough more than

18
00:01:31.688 --> 00:01:37.517
ever. Finally he huddled in the door of his cab.

19
00:01:41.499 --> 00:01:45.121
At twelve thirty he went to the door of the house to ask if his services were still

20
00:01:45.181 --> 00:01:50.304
wanted. "Yes, they'll be out pretty soon," a servant told him.

21
00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:55.267
Another forty-five minutes passed before the party finally ended.

22
00:01:57.248 --> 00:02:01.010
The two gentlemen came out and climbed into the cab without a word of apology.

23
00:02:02.191 --> 00:02:05.937
My legs were numb from standing in the cold, and I was glad to be moving.

24
00:02:07.899 --> 00:02:11.942
We dropped off the men and headed home, where Polly was waiting up for us as usual.

25
00:02:14.825 --> 00:02:18.108
By that time Jerry was coughing so hard he could barely speak.

26
00:02:18.128 --> 00:02:22.472
"Please get Jack something warm," he told his worried wife.

27
00:02:24.714 --> 00:02:27.816
She hurried inside while Jerry took off the harness and groomed me.

28
00:02:28.897 --> 00:02:31.920
Polly soon brought me a warm mash that made me feel as good as new.

29
00:02:34.164 --> 00:02:36.646
Nobody came to the stable until late the next morning.

30
00:02:39.228 --> 00:02:40.650
Finally young Harry showed up.

31
00:02:41.710 --> 00:02:44.753
He fed us, cleaned our stalls, and then left again.

32
00:02:44.773 --> 00:02:47.695
"What's going on?"

33
00:02:48.116 --> 00:02:48.916
Hotspur wondered.

34
00:02:48.936 --> 00:02:50.898
"It's not Sunday, is it?"

35
00:02:52.199 --> 00:02:53.400
"No," I said.

36
00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:54.821
"This is strange."

37
00:02:57.203 --> 00:02:58.865
Harry returned a few hours later.

38
00:02:59.265 --> 00:03:00.726
This time his sister was with him.

39
00:03:01.827 --> 00:03:02.548
She was crying.

40
00:03:05.356 --> 00:03:07.097
"Don't worry," Harry told her.

41
00:03:07.117 --> 00:03:09.238
"Father will get better."

42
00:03:09.258 --> 00:03:11.740
"But he's so sick!"

43
00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:12.800
Dolly cried.

44
00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:14.542
"What if he doesn't?"

45
00:03:15.882 --> 00:03:19.144
For two days we didn't see anyone but Harry and sometimes Dolly.

46
00:03:20.165 --> 00:03:22.186
Both children looked worried all the time.

47
00:03:24.227 --> 00:03:27.789
On the third day, Harry was in the stable when there was a tap at the door.

48
00:03:29.951 --> 00:03:32.072
It was the older cab driver known as the Governor.

49
00:03:33.788 --> 00:03:37.270
"I didn't want to bother your parents, my boy," he said to Harry.

50
00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:39.511
"How's your father doing?"

51
00:03:39.531 --> 00:03:45.135
"He's pretty sick," Harry said, his voice shaking a little.

52
00:03:46.155 --> 00:03:48.256
"The doctor says it's bronchitis."

53
00:03:48.276 --> 00:03:51.738
"Oh dear," the Governor said.

54
00:03:51.758 --> 00:03:54.060
"That can be very bad indeed!

55
00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:58.362
But if anyone can pull through, it's your father."

56
00:03:59.863 --> 00:04:01.564
The next day the Governor came back.

57
00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:07.243
When he heard that Jerry was still very ill, he offered to take Hotspur out with his own

58
00:04:07.283 --> 00:04:12.526
cab. "Jack will be all right with a week or two of rest," he told Harry.

59
00:04:12.546 --> 00:04:16.628
"You can walk him up and down the street to stretch his legs.

60
00:04:18.349 --> 00:04:20.170
But this young horse is another matter."

61
00:04:21.871 --> 00:04:23.292
"Yes," Harry admitted.

62
00:04:23.312 --> 00:04:28.155
"Hotspur is already getting restless even though I'm giving him less grain."

63
00:04:31.340 --> 00:04:36.041
The Governor offered to take Hotspur out every day and give half of what he earned to Jerry

64
00:04:36.081 --> 00:04:36.562
and Polly.

65
00:04:37.582 --> 00:04:39.102
That went on for a week or so.

66
00:04:40.223 --> 00:04:46.024
It worked out well for everyone involved, including the Governor's own horses, who got a little extra rest.

67
00:04:47.385 --> 00:04:49.285
Meanwhile Jerry was finally getting better.

68
00:04:50.485 --> 00:04:54.026
But the doctor told him he should never go back to cab work if he wanted to live

69
00:04:54.086 --> 00:04:54.787
to old age.

70
00:04:56.047 --> 00:04:59.128
One afternoon Harry was in the stable when Dolly came rushing in.

71
00:05:01.164 --> 00:05:01.844
"Who lives at Fairstowe?"

72
00:05:02.224 --> 00:05:02.704
she asked.

73
00:05:02.724 --> 00:05:06.926
"Mother just got a letter from there, and she looks very excited!"

74
00:05:06.946 --> 00:05:14.428
"Fairstowe? That's the name of the place where Mother worked before she married Father," Harry said.

75
00:05:14.448 --> 00:05:20.349
"Remember? Father said he ran into the lady who lived there last summer."

76
00:05:20.369 --> 00:05:23.550
"I wonder what she's writing about?"

77
00:05:23.930 --> 00:05:24.550
Dolly said.

78
00:05:26.151 --> 00:05:27.131
We soon found out.

79
00:05:27.891 --> 00:05:30.252
Polly's old mistress had heard about Jerry's illness.

80
00:05:31.848 --> 00:05:35.089
She wanted the whole family to come and live in the cottage on her estate!

81
00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:39.751
Her coachman was retiring soon, and Jerry could take his place.

82
00:05:41.072 --> 00:05:43.873
Hotspur and I were happy for our kind master, of course.

83
00:05:44.353 --> 00:05:45.514
But we were sad too.

84
00:05:47.134 --> 00:05:50.836
Jerry wouldn't be able to take us with him, and so we both had to be sold.
